  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2025 PS4045 Gaza Acute Crisis Joint Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Based on the most urgent needs in Gaza, as well as the consortium members&#x2019; areas of expertise, the joint response will focus on:FSL:FSC-I2: Number of people enabled to meet their basic food needsDistribution of food parcels to 1,250 of the most vulnerable families (7,450 individuals).WASH:WSH-I1: Number of people having regular access to soap to meet hygienic needsDistribution of hygiene kits and dignity kits to 1,250 vulnerable families, with a focus on girls and young women (7,450 individuals).WSH-I4: Number of people having access to sufficient and safe water for domestic use90.000 individuals benefit from the restoration and repair of water supply infrastructure and pipeline and distribution of 5,000 water jerrycans.HEALTH:HEA-I1: Number of health facilities rehabilitatedMinor rehabilitation of Juzoor&apos;s mobile medical point in the Jabalia Al-Balad area (Gaza city)HEA-I2: Number of mental health consultationsMobile health clinics will provide mental health consultations for 4,080 individuals.HEA-I5: Number of primary health care consultationsPrimary health care consultations for 71,145 individuals including follow-up referrals to GBV services and other secondary care.HEA-I7: Number of children who received community-based treatment for malaria, diarrhoea and/or acute respiratory infectionsMedical consultations specifically for children will target 7,200 children including children living with disabilities.PROTECTION:PRO-I2: Number of persons who receive an appropriate responseMHPSS and a comprehensive and coherent package of protection services tailored to meet the diverse needs of affected individuals will be provided to 11,142 people. The protection package includes the provision of case management services to assess and address individual risks and needs, as well as establishing referral pathways to ensure access to specialized services, such as medical care, legal assistance, and psychosocial support (PSS).PRO-I5: Number of children that received support specified to their needsProvision of Child Protection services tailored to the specific needs of 3200 children, including psychosocial support, individual and group counselling, case management, and referrals to appropriate services.MPC:CSH-I1: Number of people benefitting from unconditional and unrestricted cash transfersProvide Emergency MPCA to the most vulnerable households to meet their immediate needs. 2 rounds of unrestricted and unconditional cash (via e-transfer) will be provided for 550 HHs or 3,080 individuals</narrative>
  </description>
